# Living Survey: Artificial_General_Intelligence                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
## Introduction                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Artificial_General_Intelligence**.                 
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
## Theoretical Foundations & Cognitive Architectures                                                            
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
Recent scholarship has begun to rigorously redefine the architectural boundaries of AGI. Bradley (2026) proposes
a morphogenetic topological framework, arguing that autonomy and consciousness emerge from the structural       
preservation of a "Form F" against dissolution, mathematically framing AGI as an inevitable geometric property  
rather than a computational byproduct [^10.5281_zenodo.19034234]. Complementing this, Yampolskiy (2024)         
challenges the conflation of AGI with Human-Level AI (HLAI), proving that human cognition lacks the true        
generality required for AGI, thereby necessitating distinct architectural paradigms [^10.1201_9781003440260-12].
Neubauer (2021) further explores this distinction, contrasting human versus artificial intelligence concepts    
while examining how cognitive enhancements and individual psychological differences could shape the development 
of super-intelligent systems [^10.1016_j.intell.2021.101563].                                                   
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
## Safety, Alignment & Control                                                                                  
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
As AGI capabilities expand, ensuring provable safety has emerged as a critical research frontier. Tegmark and   
Omohundro (2023) argue that formal verification and mechanistic interpretability, powered by advanced AI itself,
represent the only viable path to guaranteeing that powerful AGI systems satisfy human-specified requirements   
without catastrophic failure [^10.48550_arxiv.2309.01933]. This technical safety imperative is closely tied to  
the broader question of machine consciousness. Johnson (2023) highlights the intense academic speculation       
surrounding whether AI systems can ever achieve genuine consciousness [^10.1109_mpuls.2023.3354609].            
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
## Ethics, Policy & Societal Impact                                                                             
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
                                                                                                                
The trajectory of AGI development is heavily influenced by regulatory frameworks and ethical critiques. Stahl   
and Eke (2026) critique the European Union's recent calls for AGI in healthcare, warning that the ambiguous and 
contested nature of the term AGI conflicts with the EU's precautionary principle, potentially masking           
unquantifiable risks behind funding initiatives [^10.1016_j.jrt.2026.100183]. Gebru and Torres (2024) draw a    
direct lineage between modern AGI safety rhetoric and historical Anglo-American eugenics, arguing that the      
pursuit of an undefined "beneficial AGI" centralizes power and perpetuates systemic discrimination under the    
guise of safety [^10.5210_fm.v29i4.13636]. On a macro-societal level, Hutter and Hutter (2021) outline two      
